  "definition": "In machine learning, an Epoch is one complete pass through the entire training dataset, during which model parameters are updated after each constituent batch. The number of epochs is a primary training hyperparameter: too few yield underfitting, whilst too many risk overfitting\u2014a trade-off managed by techniques such as early stopping and learning-rate scheduling.",
